{"id": "EUVD-2026-96364", "enisaUuid": "c8abee72-260f-3852-99c1-60cc60dfd16b", "description": "TencentCloud Octop through 1.0.2b6 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privileged users to read stored provider API keys via GET /api/providers and GET /api/voice/providers. Attackers can query these endpoints, which only validate the JWT, to obtain plaintext LLM and voice provider API keys and abuse the upstream provider accounts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T15:57:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/TencentCloud/Octop/pull/1507", "https://github.com/TencentCloud/Octop/pull/1265", "https://hackmd.io/@haind/octop-provider-key-cross-role-read", "https://github.com/TencentCloud/Octop/blob/eb28011249c02cafd389b2d424294c6c1b9cf422/src/octop/api/routers/providers.py#L120-L208", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/octop-through-1.0-2b6-missing-authorization-exposes-provider-api-keys-via-api-providers"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c344-c8vm-8rxv", "CVE-2026-108581"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "eeff42b7-fae0-3df9-b23a-7bab1a5dda9b", "product": {"name": "Octop", "vendor": {"name": "TencentCloud"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.2b6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "12cf33bb-0841-3740-894d-e0eeaae2df8b", "vendor": {"name": "TencentCloud"}}], "isExploited": false}